---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../../../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
import { withBase, absUrl } from '../../../site';

// Source for all kick-offs: uefa.com match API (match.uefa.com/v5/matches, competitionId=1), checked 20 Oct 2026 09:50 CEST.
const path = '/news/champions-league-tomorrow-21-oct/';
const articleLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'NewsArticle',
  headline: 'Champions League on Wednesday in Madrid: Real Madrid vs RB Leipzig and Bayern vs Arsenal',
  description: 'Real Madrid vs RB Leipzig and Bayern vs Arsenal at 21:00, LIVE at Dubliners by Sol. Leipzig fans welcome: fans meeting point, open from 12:00.',
  inLanguage: 'en',
  datePublished: '2026-10-20T10:30:00+02:00',
  dateModified: '2026-10-20T10:30:00+02:00',
  image: [absUrl('/images/dubliners-champions-night-screens-1200.webp')],
  mainEntityOfPage: absUrl(path),
  author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Dubliners Irish Pub', url: absUrl('/') },
  publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Dubliners Irish Pub', url: absUrl('/') },
};
---

<BaseLayout title={'Champions League Wed 21 Oct: Real Madrid–Leipzig | Dubliners'} description={'Real Madrid vs RB Leipzig and Bayern vs Arsenal at 21:00, LIVE at Dubliners by Sol. Leipzig fans welcome: fans meeting point, open from 12:00.'} path={path} lang="en" hreflang={{ en: '/news/champions-league-tomorrow-21-oct/', es: '/es/noticias/champions-manana-21-oct/' }} ogImage="/images/dubliners-champions-night-screens-1200.webp" extraJsonLd={articleLd}>
  <section class="hero hero-compact">
    <div class="container">
      <Breadcrumb current={'Champions League, 21 Oct'} schema />
      <h1>Champions League on Wednesday: Real Madrid vs RB Leipzig and Bayern vs Arsenal</h1>
      <p class="small"><time datetime="2026-10-20T10:30:00+02:00">Published 20 October 2026</time></p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container split">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Day two of Champions League matchday 3. On Wednesday 21 October, Real Madrid host RB Leipzig at the Bernabéu and Bayern Munich play Arsenal, both at 21:00 Madrid time. We show them LIVE on the big projector and our 8 screens, together with the rest of the night.</p>
        <h2>Leipzig fans: welcome to Madrid</h2>
        <p>Travelling from Leipzig for the game? You are very welcome at Dubliners. We are a fans meeting point in the centre of Madrid, at Calle de Espoz y Mina 7, by Puerta del Sol. <strong>Willkommen in Madrid, Leipzig-Fans!</strong> More information in German: <a href={withBase('/de/leipzig-fans-madrid/')} hreflang="de">RB-Leipzig-Fans in Madrid</a>.</p>
        <h2>Wednesday’s Champions League (Madrid time)</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>18:45</strong>: Lille vs Galatasaray · Como vs Manchester United</li>
          <li><strong>21:00</strong>: Real Madrid vs RB Leipzig · Bayern Munich vs Arsenal · Inter vs Shakhtar Donetsk · Sporting CP vs LASK · Aston Villa vs Viking · Club Brugge vs Lens · Real Betis vs Feyenoord</li>
        </ul>
        <p>All kick-off times are taken from UEFA’s fixture list and given in Madrid time.</p>
        <h2>Before the match, or instead of the stadium</h2>
        <p>We open from 12:00, so there is the whole day to meet up before heading to the Bernabéu, or to watch the game here with Real Madrid, Arsenal and Bayern fans. Metro Sol (lines 1, 2 and 3) or Sevilla (line 2).</p>
        <p>Tonight’s games are in <a href={withBase('/news/champions-league-tonight-20-oct/')}>Champions League on Tuesday 20 October</a>. The full week is on <a href={withBase('/whats-on/')}>What’s On</a>, and more about how we show football is on our <a href={withBase('/watch-football-madrid/')}>watch football in Madrid</a> page.</p>
      </div>
      <picture>
        <img class="split-photo tall" src={withBase('/images/dubliners-champions-night-screens-1200.webp')} srcset={`${withBase('/images/dubliners-champions-night-screens-800.webp')} 800w, ${withBase('/images/dubliners-champions-night-screens-1200.webp')} 1200w`} sizes="(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 720px" width="1200" height="1600" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Football match on the big screen and a TV at Dubliners, with fans watching from the tables and standing at the back of the room" />
      </picture>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
